adjudication.rationale:
In SpanFlusher.join(), the new per-process loop breaks out of the *entire* `for` when `remaining_time <= 0` (i.e., once the deadline passes):
```py
for process_index, process in self.processes.items():
    if deadline is not None:
        remaining_time = deadline - time.time()
        if remaining_time <= 0:
            break
    ...
    if isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process):
        process.terminate()
```
Because `terminate()` is only called inside the loop after waiting, any processes after the break are skipped entirely and never terminated. Previously there was only one `self.process`, and `terminate()` would still run after the wait loop even when the deadline was exceeded. This diff therefore introduces a real risk of leaving some flusher processes running past join/cleanup when `timeout` is used.
